{"name":"Tail Lights","hex":"#dd4411","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tail lights","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of tail light"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tail_lights"}],"entries":[{"title":"Automotive lighting","blocks":[{"text":"Automotive lighting is functional exterior lighting in vehicles. A motor vehicle has lighting and signaling devices mounted to or integrated into its front, rear, sides, and, in some cases, top. Various devices have the dual function of illuminating the road ahead for the driver, and making the vehicle visible to others, with indications to them of turning, slowing or stopping, etc., with lights also indicating the size of some large vehicles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Reisebus.Heck.jpg/330px-Reisebus.Heck.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Automotive_lighting","wikidata":"Q964912"},{"title":"Tail","blocks":[{"text":"The tail is the elongated section at the rear end of a bilaterian animal's body; in general, the term refers to a distinct, flexible appendage extending backwards from the midline of the torso. In vertebrate animals that evolved to lose their tails, the coccyx is the homologous vestigial of the tail. While tails are primarily considered a feature of vertebrates, some invertebrates such as scorpions and springtails, as well as snails and slugs, have tail-like appendages that are also referred to as tails."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/White-tailed_deer%2C_tail_up.jpg/330px-White-tailed_deer%2C_tail_up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tail","wikidata":"Q60960"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Foglights.jpg/500px-Foglights.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Foglights.jpg/500px-Foglights.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Selective yellow fog lights","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFoglights.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Cornering_lamp_on_Oldsmobile_98.jpg/500px-Cornering_lamp_on_Oldsmobile_98.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Cornering_lamp_on_Oldsmobile_98.jpg/500px-Cornering_lamp_on_Oldsmobile_98.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A cornering light on a 1983 Oldsmobile 98","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACornering_lamp_on_Oldsmobile_98.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/2018_Dodge_Grand_Caravan_SE_in_silver_-_detail_of_light_-_front_left.jpg/500px-2018_Dodge_Grand_Caravan_SE_in_silver_-_detail_of_light_-_front_left.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/2018_Dodge_Grand_Caravan_SE_in_silver_-_detail_of_light_-_front_left.jpg/1280px-2018_Dodge_Grand_Caravan_SE_in_silver_-_detail_of_light_-_front_left.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/2018_Dodge_Grand_Caravan_SE_in_silver_-_detail_of_light_-_front_left.jpg/500px-2018_Dodge_Grand_Caravan_SE_in_silver_-_detail_of_light_-_front_left.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Front position light lit within front light assembly on a 2018 Dodge Grand Caravan SE","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2018_Dodge_Grand_Caravan_SE_in_silver_-_detail_of_light_-_front_left.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/LED_Da